8. She found that waiting for the shower water to heat slightly by sitting in a container for hours made it more bearable. (Verbatim: "if no one was having a shower for hours that would have time to then heat up a little by very very like even just one degree okay um and that would be enough to make it just a little bit nicer")
9. She experienced extreme physical and mental stress during her jungle trek, describing it as the most stressful period of her life. (Verbatim: "i've never been more stressed in my entire life and no amount of stress seems to really compare to to that level of stress")
10. She had to complete physically demanding jungle treks lasting four to five hours daily, even if injured. (Verbatim: "i also had to do my four to five hour jungle treks every day so yeah i've never been more stressed in my entire life") [end of text]



